# Solana RPC — REQUIRED. This is a client-side, read-only dashboard: the
# value below ships to every visitor's browser in plain text (view-source,
# devtools network tab, anyone). That's inherent to the architecture, so:
#
#   - Use a key dedicated to this dashboard, not one shared with other infra.
#   - It must point at devnet only — never put a mainnet RPC/key here.
#   - Use a plan/key you're fine having scraped and hammered by strangers;
#     set its rate limit low enough that abuse can't run up a bill, and
#     rotate it if it ever gets abused.
#   - There is no code-level fallback if this is unset (see web/lib/autark.ts)
#     — the dashboard fails loudly with a styled error instead of silently
#     degrading to a shared public endpoint nobody chose.
#
# Get a free devnet key at https://helius.dev
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://devnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY

# To use public devnet instead (slower, rate-limited, fine for local dev,
# not recommended for a public deploy with multiple concurrent visitors),
# set this explicitly rather than leaving the var unset:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# Base URL this app is served at — used for absolute OG/Twitter image URLs
# and canonical links on / and /agent/[pubkey]. Must be the real deployed
# origin in production (e.g. https://autark.yourdomain.com) or shared
# profile links will unfurl with localhost URLs. Defaults to
# http://localhost:3000 for local dev.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-deployed-domain.example.com

# RUN DEMO button (web/app/api/demo/route.ts) — server-only secrets, NEVER
# prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_ or they'd ship to the browser. Generate a
# fixed provider+consumer pair with `npx tsx scripts/setup-demo-agent.ts`
# (funds SOL+USDC and registers the provider agent on devnet, one time) — it
# prints the exact lines to paste here and into your Vercel project's env
# vars. The provider agent's stake drains a little with every real slash; top
# it back up any time with the SDK's stakeDeposit instruction.
# DEMO_PROVIDER_KEYPAIR=[12,34,...]
# DEMO_CONSUMER_KEYPAIR=[56,78,...]
